%S A365313 11,13,23,25,37,47,49,59,61,71,73,83,97,107,109,121,131,157,167,169,
%T A365313 179,181,191,193,227,229,239,241,251,263,277,289,311,313,337,347,349,
%U A365313 359,361,373,383,397,409,419,421,431,433,443,457,467,479,491,503,529,541,563
%N A365313 Odd prime powers q (odd q in A246655) such that 3 is a nonzero square in the finite field F_q.
%C A365313 Prime powers q that are congruent to 1 or 11 modulo 12 (see A366526).
%C A365313 Odd prime powers q such that 3^((q-1)/2) = 1 in F_q.
%C A365313 Prime powers q such that x^2 - 3 splits into different linear factors in F_q[x].
%C A365313 Union of {p^r : p == 1, 11 (mod 12) prime, r >= 1} and {p^r : p == 5, 7 (mod 12) prime, r >= 2 even}.
%C A365313 By Hensel's lemma, also prime powers q such that 3 is a square in Q_q, where Q_{p^f} is the unique degree-f unramified extension of the p-adic field Q_p. See A085759 for a more general statement. - _Jianing Song_, Nov 24 2026
%H A365313 Jianing Song, <a href="/A365313/b365313.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A365313 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hensel%27s_lemma">Hensel's lemma</a>.
%e A365313 49 is a term since 3 = -4 = (+-2i)^2 in F_49 = F_7(i).
%t A365313 Select[Range[600], MemberQ[{1, 11}, Mod[#, 12]] && PrimePowerQ[#] &] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Mar 19 2026 *)
%o A365313 (PARI) isA365313(n) = isprimepower(n) && (n%12==1 || n%12==11)
%Y A365313 Supersequence of A097933.
%Y A365313 Cf. A246655. See A085759 for related sequences.
